      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 112.69,
      "end_seconds": 114.45,
      "duration_seconds": 1.76,
      "text": "Nothing regular, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 130.55,
      "end_seconds": 133.03,
      "duration_seconds": 2.48,
      "text": "have you had any previous surgeries?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 137.18,
      "end_seconds": 139.49,
      "duration_seconds": 2.31,
      "text": "no surgery you know no"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 140.15,
      "end_seconds": 144.3,
      "duration_seconds": 4.15,
      "text": "Do you react to any medicines or foods? Any allergies?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 145.84,
      "end_seconds": 154.47,
      "duration_seconds": 8.63,
      "text": "Years back I got bad stomach cramps from erythromycin, so I stay away from it now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 158.09,
      "end_seconds": 160.54,
      "duration_seconds": 2.45,
      "text": "I'll do your observations first"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 171.32,
      "end_seconds": 173.69,
      "duration_seconds": 2.37,
      "text": "That's it just a little longer..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 183.7,
      "end_seconds": 196.39,
      "duration_seconds": 12.69,
      "text": "Okay: height 182 centimetres, heart rate 73, BMI works out to 26.9, oxygen saturation is 99 percent, pressure 121 over 82, temperature is 36.7 degrees, weight 89 kilos."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 199.08,
      "end_seconds": 201.25,
      "duration_seconds": 2.17,
      "text": "shall I start the examination?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 209.98,
      "end_seconds": 211.58,
      "duration_seconds": 1.6,
      "text": "fine by me"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 213.26,
      "end_seconds": 215.59,
      "duration_seconds": 2.33,
      "text": "hold that that for a second"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 233.04,
      "end_seconds": 238.52,
      "duration_seconds": 5.48,
      "text": "There is an expanding ring-shaped red patch about eight centimetres across on the thigh."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 242.39,
      "end_seconds": 253.51,
      "duration_seconds": 11.12,
      "text": "You can relax now. So So where does that leave us? I can't pin this down yet. We're looking at early Lyme disease or cellulitis."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 254.51,
      "end_seconds": 257.76,
      "duration_seconds": 3.25,
      "text": "do you think it's something serious?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 258.45,
      "end_seconds": 277.18,
      "duration_seconds": 18.73,
      "text": "I understand the worry at the moment I'd say it's early Lyme disease, and and we'll watch how it goes i'll start you on doxycycline, 100 milligrams, twice a day, twenty-one days you take it by mouth it's for early Lyme disease"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 277.94,
      "end_seconds": 280.03,
      "duration_seconds": 2.09,
      "text": "Fine, I'll begin it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 280.82,
      "end_seconds": 296.76,
      "duration_seconds": 15.94,
      "text": "Take the doxycycline with food and avoid strong sun. Please don't wait if the symptoms get worse. That's when to be seen urgently. Let's plan a check in three weeks. Have I covered everything you wanted?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 298.61,
      "end_seconds": 301.08,
      "duration_seconds": 2.47,
      "text": "that's clear um thanks"
    },
